From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:02:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] bundler: support centralized context reuse policy

Add a disabled-by-default root-application bundling policy that emits
Convex's existing boolean experimental_reuseContext marker for isolate
entries. Keep reviewed exceptions in a centralized reasoned map and fail
when exclusions are stale or source output carries a competing marker.

Allow applications targeting a backend with typed context-reuse policy to
enable reviewed HTTP-action graphs and explicitly selected ordinary isolate
action entries independently. Ordinary-action entries must be unique,
normalized root isolate paths and must not overlap exclusions. Omitted
action settings retain fresh ordinary actions and the existing upstream
marker behavior.

Leave imported components, Node modules, schema bundles, and auth
configuration bundles unchanged. Document the backend compatibility
contract and cover boolean and typed marker insertion, exclusions,
conflicts, stale paths, and independent action permissions.

Under the same opt-in, group forwarding-only entries with identical ordered
static chunk imports. Emit a fixed initializer importing all members and
carry its canonical dependency path in the typed policy. Group entries
separately by ordinary-action permission so initialization never includes
unreviewed action entries. Allow ordinary-action grouping to be disabled
while preserving per-entry reuse.

Supporting backends use the initializer for separate database and ordinary-
action cache kinds and validate every member. Older typed-policy backends
retain per-entry reuse, and boolean-only backends run grouped entries fresh.
Keep HTTP action keys, exclusions, and source-policy ownership intact.
Bind group identity to member contents and dependencies, fit generated paths
within the backend component limit, and exercise the emitted ESM graph.
